.\" sessionintent.1
.\" Manual page for sessionintent
.\"
.TH SESSIONINTENT 1 "2026-09-18" "sessionintent 0.3.3" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
sessionintent \- A declarative session orchestration system for Linux desktops

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sessionintent
[\fIGLOBAL\fR]... \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR]...

.SH DESCRIPTION
SessionIntent is a session orchestration system that switches between
different "intent-based modes" that automatically launch, reuse, and
organize applications across workspaces. Backends are auto-detected
(GNOME, KDE, Hyprland, Sway, wlroots, EWMH).

.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config \fIPATH\fR
Use a custom configuration file instead of the default.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-dev
Enable developer mode: print commands instead of executing them.
.TP
.BR \-\-backend " \fINAME\fR
Workspace backend override: gnome, ewmh, kde, hyprland, sway, wlroots.

.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR "apply " \fIMODE\fR
Apply a specific mode directly, bypassing the UI selector.
.TP
.BR "preview " \fIMODE\fR
Preview a mode (workspaces and apps) without applying it.
.TP
.BR select
Prompt for mode selection via UI (requires wofi or rofi).
This is the default behavior when no command is provided.
.TP
.BR list
List available modes from configuration.
.TP
.BR status
Show current session status (mode, power state, dev mode).
.TP
.BR panic
Clear current session state without killing any processes.
.TP
.BR quit
Gracefully close managed applications (sends SIGTERM).
.TP
.BR clear
Clear state files only (without touching applications).
.TP
.BR kill
Force kill managed applications (sends SIGKILL).
.TP
.BR suspend
Suspend session (pause mode switching).
.TP
.BR init
Initialize default configuration files and workspace extension.
.TP
.BR setup
Run the interactive app setup wizard.
.TP
.BR "scan " [\fB\-f\fR|\fB\-\-force\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-cache\fR] [\fB\-\-clear\-cache\fR]
Rescan installed apps.
.TP
.BR reload
Reload configuration files.
.TP
.BR version
Display version information and exit.

.SH EXAMPLES
.SS "Basic Usage"
.TP
.I "sessionintent select"
Select a session mode using the UI (default behavior).
.TP
.I "sessionintent apply work"
Apply the 'work' mode directly.
.TP
.I "sessionintent --dev apply work"
See what commands would be executed without running them.
.SS "Session Control"
.TP
.I "sessionintent panic"
Clear the current session state.
.TP
.I "sessionintent quit"
Gracefully close all managed applications.
.SS "Configuration"
.TP
.I "sessionintent init"
Initialize default configuration files.
.TP
.I "sessionintent scan --force"
Rescan installed apps, ignoring the cache.

.SH CONFIGURATION
Version 2 configs are required (version 1 is migrated in memory with a
notice). See docs/MIGRATION.md.

Configuration files are located in:
.IP
~/.config/sessionintent/config.yaml
.br
~/.config/sessionintent/apps.yaml

.SH REQUIREMENTS
.IP
\- Python 3.10+
.IP
\- PyYAML
.IP
\- wofi or rofi (for UI selection)
.IP
\- A supported desktop (GNOME, KDE, Hyprland, Sway, wlroots) or X11/EWMH

